    <h1>What you get at different types of Goa hotels</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Property style changes the shape of a trip. A resort may bring more facilities on site; a small independent stay may offer a more intimate scale; a city base can make sense when the beach is not the main plan. These are differences in setting and offer, not a price or quality ranking.</p>

    <h2>Resort-scale stays: more of the trip can happen on property</h2>
    <p>The resort entries in this shortlist vary in beach access and facilities. <a href="/hotels/itc-grand-goa/">ITC Grand Goa</a> lists direct access to Arossim Beach, a multi-level pool, spa, six restaurants and a children’s play zone. <a href="/hotels/taj-fort-aguada-goa/">Taj Fort Aguada</a> lists direct Sinquerim Beach access and resort facilities. At <a href="/hotels/alila-diwa-goa/">Alila Diwa Goa</a>, the official page lists a shuttle to Gonsua Beach; <a href="/hotels/w-goa-vagator/">W Goa</a> is a Vagator resort with several pools and dining venues.</p>
    <p>The trade-off is not simply “more is better.” Check which facilities you will use, whether the beach is reached directly or by shuttle, and whether the hotel’s location fits the rest of your plans. A large on-site offer may matter less if you expect to spend most of each day elsewhere.</p>

    <h2>Small independent stays: compare scale and setting</h2>
    <p><a href="/hotels/ahilya-by-the-sea/">Ahilya by the Sea</a> describes nine rooms across three independent villas in Nerul, with two pools. Its scale differs from the larger resorts, while its locality is still a specific North Goa base rather than a hotel on every nearby beach.</p>
    <p><a href="/hotels/amrapali-house-of-grace/">Amrapali • House of Grace</a> is an independent stay in Goa Velha, with riverside gardens and a slow-cooking kitchen described by the property. It is not beachfront, so it suits a different itinerary from a coast-first resort. The official information checked does not state its room count; we do not estimate one.</p>

    <h2>Tourism residencies and city bases: check the exact offer</h2>
    <p><a href="/hotels/calangute-residency/">Calangute Residency</a> is listed by Goa Tourism Development Corporation with cottages and suites, a travel desk and room service. The current listing does not establish whether its pool is operating. <a href="/hotels/panaji-residency/">Panaji Residency</a> is a city property behind the Old Secretariat, with room categories and services listed by GTDC. These provide alternatives to resort-led beach stays, but do not assume a lower price: this site does not collect live rates or compare like-for-like room costs.</p>

    <h2>Compare the details that matter to your trip</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Beach access:</strong> distinguish direct access, a shuttle and a nearby beach from the hotel’s exact locality.</li>
      <li><strong>Facilities:</strong> check the official source for the amenities you plan to use, then confirm current operation for your dates.</li>
      <li><strong>Scale:</strong> compare room count or property footprint only where the source states it.</li>
      <li><strong>Trip pattern:</strong> decide whether you want to stay on site, move between areas, or base yourself in a city.</li>
      <li><strong>Terms:</strong> confirm room inclusions, transport and cancellation conditions with the hotel before booking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The hotel profiles link to the official property information and show when each source was checked. See the <a href="/compare/">side-by-side hotel comparison</a>, the <a href="/guides/north-goa-vs-south-goa/">North Goa vs South Goa guide</a>, or the <a href="/guides/before-booking-goa-hotel/">seven-point booking checklist</a>.</p>
